TASK: HYPERPARAMETER RECOMMENDATION
Based on the profile above, recommend three generation hyperparameters:

- ctx_size_pct: the percentage (integer, 5-50) of the training split to show the LLM as
  real-data context/exemplars. Lower values favour generation novelty; higher values
  favour structural anchoring. Sparse, high-cardinality, or highly skewed datasets
  typically benefit from a higher context percentage.
- strategy: the context-row sampling strategy, one of "random", "dense" (rows with the
  fewest missing values), or "diverse" (maximally spread out via K-Means clustering).
  Datasets with high sparsity or many outliers typically benefit from "dense" or
  "diverse" over plain "random".
- temperature: the LLM sampling temperature (float, 0.1-1.0). Lower values favour
  structural fidelity and consistency; higher values favour diversity and novelty.
  Datasets with strong fairness/disparate-impact concerns benefit from a lower
  temperature to keep generation tightly anchored to the observed distribution.

